MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The epoxy felt like a natural choice because I have bought repair tapes and vinyl cement; another adhesive could help with small repairs if it works on the materials involved.",
    "The heat shrink tubing complements my crimp connectors by helping insulate and protect compatible wire repairs. The connector kit also fits that interest, although I do not need such a large replenishment now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Buying hose clamps does not mean I need a water pump, and buying electrical connectors does not establish a need for heavy battery lugs or replacement multimeter leads.",
    "Grinding discs, strong magnets, and measuring gauges each serve particular tasks that my purchases do not show I currently need to do. Being useful for repairs in general is not enough for me to choose them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My practical repair purchases seem to have been stretched into an interest in almost any workshop supply.",
    "Shared words such as hose, wire, or electrical seem to count too much when the actual use, required equipment, and dimensions differ."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I care about whether an item works with the materials, wire sizes, and equipment I actually have; specialized fittings need more evidence of a match.",
    "My purchases are spread across separate tasks over several years. An older connector assortment does not by itself mean I need another, especially a much larger kit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in practical repairs but often assumed specific projects and replenishment needs that my history does not establish."
}
